\date{2024-07-26}
\taxon{Theorem}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\meta{source}{Theorem 3.1.6 of [[myers-riley-2023]]}
\import{common}

\p{Suppose the crisp type family #{{G :_\flat I \to \Type}} [detects continuity](fb-0046) for #{{\flat \dashv \sharp}} and assume given a crisp map #{{f :_\flat X \to Y}}. Then #{f} is an [[hott-000U]] if (and only if) #{{\flat f : \flat X \to \flat Y}} is an equivalence and for all #{{i :_\flat I}}, the map
##{\flat(f \o \blank) : \flat(G_i \to X) \to \flat(G_i \to Y)}
is an equivalence.}
